---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import ScoreCard from '../../components/ScoreCard.astro';
import MetaScoreBadge from '../../components/MetaScoreBadge.astro';
import VerdictBox from '../../components/VerdictBox.astro';
import CTA from '../../components/CTA.astro';
import DisclosureBlock from '../../components/DisclosureBlock.astro';
import LastVerified from '../../components/LastVerified.astro';
import FAQ from '../../components/FAQ.astro';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';

const app = appBySlug('flowkey');
const title = 'How Much Does Flowkey Cost in 2026? Full Price Breakdown';
const description =
  'Flowkey costs $24.99/month or $149.99/year for Premium (7-day free trial, card required), with a cheaper Classic tier at $99.99/year. Full breakdown of every plan, the discount reality, and how it compares to Simply Piano, Skoove, and Pianote.';
---

<BaseLayout title={`${title} | ${SITE.name}`} description={description}>
  <PageHeader title={title} crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'How much does Flowkey cost?' }]}>
    Flowkey costs <strong>$24.99/month</strong> or <strong>$149.99/year</strong> for the full Premium plan,
    with a 7-day free trial (card required) — plus a cheaper Classic tier at $99.99/year for
    course-only learners. It remains the highest-rated app we track
    (MetaScore <MetaScoreBadge app={app} showSources={false} />) at a mid-range price.
    Full breakdown below.
    <ScoreCard app={app} linkReview slot="aside" />
  </PageHeader>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose">
    <h2>Flowkey prices in 2026</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Premium monthly:</strong> $24.99/month — full song library (pop, film, TV, classical), the flexible option, but the worst value: about $300/year if you stay on it.</li>
      <li><strong>Premium annual:</strong> $149.99/year — $12.50/month-equivalent, and the plan almost every committed learner picks.</li>
      <li><strong>Classic:</strong> about $16.99/month or $99.99/year — the course library plus classical songs, without the licensed pop/film catalog. The budget way into Flowkey.</li>
      <li><strong>Family:</strong> about $37.99/month or $224.99/year — Premium for up to 5 profiles.</li>
      <li><strong>Free trial:</strong> 7 days of Premium, card required. Cancel before day 7 to avoid being charged.</li>
      <li><strong>No permanent free tier.</strong> After the trial ends, you pay or lose access.</li>
      <li><strong>Run by Yamaha.</strong> Flowkey is a Yamaha company — the app is backed by one of the largest instrument makers in the world, so your subscription is not funding a fragile startup.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>The monthly vs. annual math</h2>
    <p>
      The break-even is fast: 6 × $24.99 = $149.94, essentially the annual price. If you will practice for more
      than 6 months, the annual plan is cheaper than month-to-month. Committed learners should buy
      the year; casual tinkerers should start on the trial and reassess. On a tight budget, Classic at
      $99.99/year undercuts every mainstream course app except Piano Tree's promo pricing.
    </p>
    <h2>The discount reality: the sticker price is a ceiling</h2>
    <p>
      Flowkey's "real" price is whatever the current discount is. The app runs frequent promotions and
      third-party discount sales — the $149.99/yr Premium sticker price is a ceiling, not a floor. Check our
      <a href="/deals/">deals page</a> before buying; you may never need to pay full price.
    </p>
    <h2>Flowkey vs. competitor prices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Simply Piano:</strong> $169.90/yr — $20 more than Flowkey Premium, and rated lower (MetaScore 8.6 vs 8.9). You pay extra for a more structured beginner curriculum.</li>
      <li><strong>Skoove:</strong> $149.99/yr — the same price as Flowkey Premium, with real-instructor support bundled but a much smaller song library.</li>
      <li><strong>Yousician:</strong> $139.99/yr — $10 cheaper, covers piano plus guitar, ukulele, bass, and singing, but its piano curriculum is shallower.</li>
      <li><strong>Piano Marvel:</strong> $129.99/yr — $20 cheaper than Flowkey Premium, MIDI-focused, but a smaller user base and lower ratings.</li>
      <li><strong>Pianote:</strong> $279/yr — nearly double Flowkey's price, for real teachers, live Q&amp;A, and a genuine advanced path.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Context: $149.99/year is roughly one-twentieth the cost of a year of weekly private piano lessons. Every app here is cheap next to a teacher — the real question is which app you will actually open.</p>
    <h2>Hidden costs and things to watch</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Auto-renewal</strong> after the trial: the card you enter on day 1 gets charged on day 8 unless you cancel.</li>
      <li><strong>Advanced players hit a ceiling.</strong> The lesson path runs out quickly for serious players — if that is you, you are buying a $149.99 stepping stone, not a multi-year tool. <a href="/pianote-review/">Pianote</a> is the honest upgrade path.</li>
      <li><strong>Course depth for absolute beginners.</strong> Flowkey's song-first approach is its strength, but the course structure is thinner than Simply Piano's for day-one beginners.</li>
      <li><strong>Keyboard costs extra.</strong> Like every app here, Flowkey assumes you have a piano or keyboard — mic input works with any instrument, no cable needed, but you still need the instrument.</li>
    </ul>
    <VerdictBox title="Is the price fair?">
      At $149.99/yr, Flowkey Premium is fairly priced for what it is: the highest MetaScore (8.9) at a
      mid-range annual price, with a genuine budget tier (Classic, $99.99/yr) underneath. It only fails the
      value test for advanced players who will outgrow the curriculum. Full verdict:
      <a href="/is-flowkey-worth-it/">is Flowkey worth it in 2026?</a>
    </VerdictBox>
    <CTA app={app} label="Try Flowkey free for 7 days" />
    <p>More: <a href="/flowkey-review/">full Flowkey review</a> · <a href="/simply-piano-vs-flowkey/">Simply Piano vs Flowkey</a> · <a href="/flowkey-vs-pianote/">Flowkey vs Pianote</a> · <a href="/flowkey-alternatives/">alternatives</a></p>
    <FAQ items={[
      { q: 'How much is Flowkey per month?', a: '$24.99/month for Premium (full song library), or about $16.99/month for the course-only Classic tier. Annual plans cut both substantially.' },
      { q: 'How much is Flowkey per year?', a: '$149.99/year for Premium at sticker price — but Flowkey runs frequent promotions, so check the deals page before buying; you may never need to pay full price. Classic is $99.99/year.' },
      { q: 'Is there a Flowkey free trial?', a: 'Yes — 7 days of Premium, card required. Cancel before day 7 to avoid being charged. There is no permanent free tier.' },
      { q: 'Is Flowkey cheaper than Simply Piano?', a: 'Yes — Flowkey Premium costs $149.99/yr vs Simply Piano\u2019s $169.90/yr, and Flowkey carries the higher MetaScore (8.9 vs 8.6).' },
      { q: 'Can I use Flowkey on my phone and computer?', a: 'Yes — one subscription covers iOS, Android, and Web, and it works with mic or MIDI input on all of them. You still need your own piano or keyboard.' },
    ]} />
    <DisclosureBlock />
    <LastVerified />
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
